[Round 5/8 | Implementer | 622.9s | 0/400k] The remaining large cost is failed try-style calls: native counts show millions of `EMPTY`/`FULL` attempts that still acquire a lock. I’m adding cache-isolated availability hints updated at the existing publication/reservation linearization points. A false hint is never trusted after lock acquisition; the fast return is used only for a stable empty/full state, while the authoritative heap/free-stack checks remain under their original locks. This preserves reservation-aware semantics and the split lock behavior.

