[Round 5/8 | Implementer | 738.8s | 0/400k] The three long runs show the availability fast path itself is correct but can let empty consumers spin so aggressively that successful throughput falls (hundreds of millions of empty attempts). I’m adding a scheduler-friendly backoff only on the lock-free `EMPTY`/`FULL` hint returns; it still returns the status immediately without waiting for queue state, and it should let the opposite side reach the publication/recycle locks under host oversubscription.

