[Round 5/8 | Implementer | 527.8s | 0/400k] The full-duration runs show the dominant failure mode is lock contention/starvation, not heap correctness: one repetition can let producers or consumers dominate, producing large `FULL`/`EMPTY` counts. I’m evaluating the existing queue’s natural publication-availability fast path (mirroring its already-present free-slot hint) to avoid taking the publication lock for a stable empty heap; I’ll retain it only if the trusted scenarios remain linearizable and the gain is substantial.

